// The control for wolf-lang#431's gate, and the reason the gate is not
// simply "no task env is ever a frame slot".
//
// Here `main` both OPENS the scope and spawns into it, so the frame
// that packs the capture record is the frame that joins — which is the
// premise `pack_task_env`'s frame-slot arm is written on, and it holds.
// This program runs correctly on every tier and every profile.
//
// It is in the tree so the gate beside it can be seen GREEN as well as
// red: a checker that flagged this too would be red for a reason that
// is not the bug.

fn main() -> !int {
    scope work {
        work.spawn(fn() { print("task-7") })
    }
    0
}
